@divyaramanathan Sorry for the late reply! We would appreciate if someone like you could take a stab at this.

There is now a `Repository.issueTemplates` GraphQL connection that returns a list of IssueTemplate objects. Our original templates implementation predates this API, so we opted to read the templates from disk instead. This, of course, does not work with `-R`.

My preferred solution would be to use the API _both_ when `-R` was passed and when it wasn't passed. See `pkg/cmd/issue/create/create.go` for existing code that uses `githubtemplate`, but should use API calls instead. You can try prototyping up these API calls!

For pull request templates, we still have to read files from disk (i.e. use the old approach) because there is no `Repository.pullRequestTemplates` GraphQL API.

@samcoe I've reclassified this as a bug, even though the original code is working as intended, since I feel that issue/PR templates should behave the same regardless of whether `-R` was used.
